// =====================================================================
// notes-in.codebox   (goes in an event-rate codebox — no tilde — inside
// the rnbo~, beside belief-cloud.codebox)
//
// Turns MIDI notes into the shared `held` table that the grain cloud
// reads. Each pitch's slot holds 0 while the key is up, or a press stamp
// (1, 2, 3, … counting every press) while it is down. The stamps let the
// cloud admit a chord's notes in the order they were played even though
// they land in the same instant.
//
// in1 = pitch (hot, the leftmost inlet), in2 = velocity (cold). [notein]
// sends velocity before pitch (right to left), so in2 is already set when
// in1 fires. A note-on with velocity 0 counts as a release.
//
// UNVERIFIED: the poke argument order. The codebox reference shows
// poke(buf, index, value); if the table fills with nonsense, swap to
// poke(buf, value, index) — the gen order — in the two lines below.
//
// PATCHER WIRING REQUIRED: [data held 128]; [notein] outlet 0 → in1,
// outlet 1 → in2. out1 echoes the stamp for a [print] while debugging.
// =====================================================================

@state held = buffer("held");
@state count = 0;

let pitch = floor(clamp(in1, 0, 127));
let stamp = 0;
if (in2 > 0) {
    count += 1;
    stamp = count;
}
poke(held, pitch, stamp);
out1 = stamp;
